Due to the extremely heavy traffic on this list, I won't be on it 
very long.  Send all responses to oceania@terminus.intermind.net.  

In _The Fountainhead_, Ayn Rand says, "...the only way in which we 
can have any law is to have as little of it as possible.  I see no 
ethical standard by which to measure the whole unethical conception 
of a State, except in the amount of time, of thought, of money, of 
effort and of obedience, which a society extorts from its every 
member.  Its value and its civilization are in inverse ratio to that 
extortion." 

Any examination of America by this standard shows that we live in an 
exceptionally unethical country.  About 47% of our gross national 
product is dedicated to government, about $3 trillion each year.  Too 
much time, thought, effort, and obedience is also extorted by the 
various levels of American government in the areas of religion, 
investment, censorship, privacy, sexuality, and in our choices for 
our bodies after "death," to name only a few.  Therefore, the value 
and civilization of America are pathetically low, due to its high 
level of extortion.  

Every hour spent by every activist interested in preserving freedom 
in any or all areas of American life must be added to that extortion, 
must be seen as an opportunity cost of outrageous proportions.  And 
fight though we each may, we are seeing a consistent regression 
across the country, freedoms lost due to election fraud, the growth 
of bureaucracies, and the incompetence (or malice) of our elected 
officials in failing to resist threats to freedom.  

The day has long passed when those who want to preserve their freedom 
must join together to create a new haven for freedom.  Though many 
will still struggle to stem the tide of repression in America, many 
more must work to create a new home for freedom, a better one, where 
the extortion of the State is limited by removing its power to tax, 
where the freedom to act is preserved by a superior Constitution 
protected by people who share the common goal of living free.  

If you want to live in a country where people are free to live as 
they please, protected by a well-written Constitution and each other, 
please help us found one.  We are the Atlantis Project, and we are 
founding a new nation called Oceania.  We have a flag, an Internet 
list server, a FTP site, a WWW site, a quarterly newsletter, a body 
